Z||000009||Kelvin Vivian||04-09-2001||03:02 AM||||This is good to hear, I too just received a replacement subwoofer speaker that I ordered from him... I originally looked him up because of a comment "fierodave" had made in his posts of his newly painted 87 burgundy GT, in which he thanked Rodney for his replacement subwoofer speaker and that it worked great... I can't wait to get mine home and hook it up....<P>Moreover, I ordered an extra gasket that I thought I needed, but didn't... Mr. Rodney Dickman clarified my order with me over email before he charged me... Excellent, individualized service INDEED.<P>The replacement subwoofer speaker is going to be going into the 87 SE 4-cyl. <P>I also ordered two "headlamp kit" upgrade kits from the Fiero Store. I received prompt shipment on these goods. The kits come with either blue, gold, or white tint halogen bulbs. I decided to get white tint bulbs. My other choice would've been blue, but seems like blue tint headlights are more at home on luxury cars. I can't wait to see what my Fieros look like with these installed...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402874&Sequence=1&res=high"> <BR>88 GT, 5-spd<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd||||reg||1
Z||000010||Dave Gunsul||04-09-2001||09:56 PM||||Darell Morse does some great<BR>work too!<BR>He ports: T-bodies and upper plenums,<BR>exhuast manifolds, heads, and is<BR>porting a lower intake for me right<BR>now!<BR>He also makes strut tower braces and<BR>many other things for our beloved little<BR>car all at reasonable prices.<BR>You can email him at: morse86@aol.com<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000011||william_thorniii||04-09-2001||11:02 PM||||I intend to salute many of the wonderful folks that contribute to the Fiero community through service, advice, knowledge and many other positive ways.  Not all sell parts or services, but all bring abundant offerings to the table of our Fiero community.  <P>I have purchased many things for my various Fiero's over the years.  As has already been mentioned Rodney Dickman has been a real pleasure to deal with.  He even helped me out of a poor headlight rebuild decision.  <P>Mark Corbin (author of Fiero Spotters Guide) undoubtedly sells the most useful tool to the Fiero owner.  This small green booklet is chalked full of useful information.  <P>Terry Owens/George Miller/Fiero Shop are great to deal with.  Their clutch is of impeccable quality and reasonably priced.  I only wish that I lived closer to cali.<P>Ed/Rosie/Jeremy et. al @ The Fiero Factory in Toney AL are possibly the greatest Fiero resource out there.  If you belong to any of the Fiero list servers you recognize them as the encyclopedia of stock Fiero mechanics (and 60 degree v-6 swaps/upgrades).  Great folks that will go out of their way to help every body.  <P>Ross @ Street Dreams dealt with my constant pestering about drop spindles.  He produced an excellent product at an adequate price.  <P>suspension.com... the absolute best place to buy poly.  <P>Steve @ whalentire.com... the best place to order wheels/tires.  Steve is a great guy that wants to move wheels.  <P>Paul Vargyas (or however his last name is spelled) - A great guy that helped me out with some rare Fiero literature.<P>theogre [wt3 offers thanks] [theogre throws a boulder] was once a source of humor with his portrayal of his name, but now has become known on the forum as the technical wizard (who once limited himself to the DIS Duke, but has now branched out to the 2.8L) behind many electrical and mechanical problems that debilitate our often annoying cars.  <P>Terryk is a wealth of great knowledge regarding the electrical systems of not only our cars, but also many others especially anything with 4 camshafts.  <P>TwistT, MWS & Will for suspension theories.<P>V8 Archie for many of the products and services he offers.  All of his offerings are available at a very reasonable price.  Also he is typically to discuss performing an engine swap, which is remarkable since that is the majority of his business.<P>Paul McKibben is a great value to the community.  Even if he did not produce great Fiero graphics, he has compiled one of the most useful Fiero sites on the net.  <P>"Dr" Joe McGee was a great guy that helped many folks find the exact Fiero they were looking for.  He helped me find my 86 SE project car in Freehold NJ... last I heard he was forced out of the Fiero community due to health problems.  <P>FieroDave has put up with many, many, many calls from me on various vehicles he has had for sale.  I am still kicking myself for passing up on not one, not two, but three of his cars that were much better off than what I settled on.  <P>SuperX Motorsports - I have to give him credit for seeing the new gauge bezels through production.  I presented a unique problem to him and he did his best to get it solved.  <P>TOM was a great value to this forum.  He was known for selling many parts cheap or even giving them away.  Personal issues contributed to him leaving the forum and possibly the entire Fiero community.  <P>Ashby Arnette is a true southern gentleman.  Fiero's are more than a hobby with him, they are a good part of his income.  One wonders how though with how little he charges for his parts.  <P>Mike Valentine/mr fiero is a great guy to buy parts from or ask advice of.  I think that he cut a per pound deal with fiero56 last year at the swap meet (in other words, 56 bought in bulk).  Mike even through in an EGR valve that I needed for my 86.  <P>Eddie Snaauw produced the most beautiful interior kit I have ever seen.  Then he sold the molds at an easily recoupable cost because he wanted to see them in Fiero's.  When his first deal looked like it might go sour, he offered a back up set of molds at an extremely reasonable price to ensure that Fiero owners would be able to purchase his dash kit.  <P>fiero56, fiero87ec05, FIEROWIFE, bengal4, BOILERMAKER, chadman, dalelee, monkeyman, 2m4 Dale... and all of the others that are local and make efforts to get together to help each other out and just have fun.  <P>And most importantly... Cliff Pennock.  Think of all of the time, energy and $ that he gives to each and every one of us here through the Forum.  It is and always will be an invaluable tool to each and every Fiero owner.  <P>I could go on about valuable form members all night (DXR, Phil, stimpy, GTB...) but I will spare you all.  <P>William T. Thorn, III<BR> -"Just call me Tolstoy"||||reg||1
